<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>subracting irrational numbers</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Simplify the following expression, giving your answer in the form \(k\sqrt{m}\), where \(m\) is as small as possible.</p>
\[ \sqrt{@x@} - \sqrt{@y@} \]
<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p>
<p>[[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>

<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Simplify \(\sqrt{@x@}\).</p>
\[ \sqrt{@x@} = \sqrt{{@a2@} \times {@n@}} = \sqrt{@a2@} \times \sqrt{@n@} = {@a@}\sqrt{@n@} \]

<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Simplify \(\sqrt{@y@}\).</p>
\[ \sqrt{@y@} = \sqrt{{@b2@} \times {@n@}} = \sqrt{@b2@} \times \sqrt{@n@} = {@b@}\sqrt{@n@} \]

<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Subtract the like terms. Both roots now have the same irrational part \(\sqrt{@n@}\), so we subtract the coefficients:</p>
\[ {@a@}\sqrt{@n@} - {@b@}\sqrt{@n@} = ({@a@} - {@b@})\sqrt{@n@} = {@c@}\sqrt{@n@} \]

<p><strong>Answer:</strong> \( {@c@}\sqrt{@n@} \)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
